PATCH 563: the HUD number formatter -- 0000:02e8, its UNPROMOTED emitter 0000:030b, and the CRT digit
chain 0f69:5d8b (FUN_1000_541b / 54ac / 54b4 / 54c2).  "GOALS REMAINING:+U".

The mission supervisor prints the objective count with `1a655 mov $0x1f8c,%si ; lcall 0:2e8` and copies
the two bytes at DGROUP:0x1f8f into the HUD text at es:0x2d8e (patch 550's site).  The original shows
"13"; the port shows "+U" -- whatever stale bytes the buffer held, because nothing ever writes it:

  * 02e8 installs a per-character callback in the CRT printer's far pointer [0x684]:[0x686] --
    0000:030b = `mov %al,(%si) ; inc %si ; lret` -- calls 0f69:5d8b (= FUN_1000_541b), restores the
    pointer and NUL-terminates at the ADVANCED SI.  030b was never promoted (board:0015 -- the icall table
    has 0x31c but not 0x30b), so the far call through [0x684] resolved to nothing; and the decompile
    wrote the NUL at the buffer START and pushed `unaff_CS` into [0x686].
  * 541b converts AX to BCD -- DX = ten-thousands, CX = the other four digits packed by `add $0x10,%ch`
    / `inc %ch` / `add $0x10,%cl` / `add %ax,%cx` -- forces byte[0x2672]=1 (no leading-zero blanking:
    always five characters, which is why a5dc copies buffer+3), then emits DL via 54c2 and CX via 54ac.
    Ghidra kept the digit-count loops, never packed CX, and passed `unaff_CS` to 54ac.
  * 54ac -> 54b4 -> 54c2 is a FALL-THROUGH chain (`push %ax ; mov %ah,%al ; call next ; pop %ax` and
    then falling into `next` with AL): four digits, two digits, one digit.  Ghidra modelled every
    fall-through operand as `unaff_CS` and called the callback with NO argument -- AL (the character)
    and SI (the cursor) are both implicit register carries.

SI is carried untouched from 02e8's caller through the whole chain and advanced only by 030b.  It is
modelled as `g_fist_02e8_si` (a DGROUP near offset, the precedent being g_fist_0578_bx / g_fist_b1df_ax
for a18e's and b1df's implicit register returns), seeded by 02e8 from its host-pointer argument
(every caller passes &DAT_1000_dfXX) and used by 030b to write dg[si]; AL is passed positionally.

Callers of 02e8 besides a5dc: the per-vehicle ammo readouts (`FUN_0000_02e8(word[...+0xad], &DAT_1000_df8c)`
at fist.c:65162 and its siblings) -- the "8888" placeholders on the cockpit's ammo counters are the
same stale buffer.  54d8/54e0/54e8 are a parallel DX-emitting chain reached by other formatters and are
not touched here.

